  "data": {
    "accession": "PXD041908",
    "title": "Targeting APEX2 to the mRNA encoding fatty acid synthase β in yeast identifies proteins that bind and control its translational efficiency in the cell cycle",
    "additionalAttributes": [],
    "projectDescription": "To understand how the translation of FAS1, encoding fatty acid synthase, peaks late in the cell cycle, we identified proteins that bind the FAS1 transcript in a cell cycle-dependent manner. We used dCas13d-APEX2 fusions to target FAS1 and label nearby proteins, which were then identified by mass spectrometry.",
    "sampleProcessingProtocol": "To isolate the biotinylated proteins for mass spectrometry, 0.2 mL of beads (Dynabeads™ MyOne™ Streptavidin C1; ThermoFisher, Cat#: 65001) were added to each tube, and Incubated on a rotisserie mixer for 1 h at room temperature. A magnetic rack was used to isolate the beads and remove the supernatant. The beads were washed twice with 10 mL TBS, 2 M urea, pH 7.5, once with 10 ml 0.1 M ammonium carbonate pH 7.7,  and resuspended in 0.5 ml 0.1 M ammonium carbonate pH 7.7. The samples described above were processed for ‘on-bead’ tryptic proteolysis LC-MS/MS mass spectrometry as described previously (Fukuyama et al, 2012). The prepared tryptic peptides were analyzed by a nano-reverse-phase liquid chromatography (LC) electrospray ionization tandem mass spectrometry (MS) system, consisting of an UltiMate 3000 Nano LC System and an LTQ-Orbitrap Elite mass spectrometer (Thermo Fisher, San Jose, CA, USA). Peptide sequences were identified by Mascot software (Matrix Science, Boston, MA, USA), by comparing the mass spectra with the expected S. cerevisiae library.",
    "dataProcessingProtocol": "The converted output file from each of the 18 experiments was named according to the strain used (strain 244 for FAS1-1 cells, 245 for FAS1-2 cells, or 246 for FAS1-3 cells), whether it was from the G1 or G2 phase, and replicate (A, B, or C). To identify proteins that were preferentially associated with the FAS1 mRNA in the G1 phase or in the G2 phase, each strain was analyzed separately with the robust bootstrap ANOVA.",
    "projectTags": [],
    "keywords": [
      "Yeast; lc-ms/ms; proximity labeling"
    ],
